 "decoded_text": "The function `ccm_finish_reduced` takes a `tag_len` parameter and uses it directly in a `memcpy` call on line 10 without validating it against the size of the source buffer `full_tag` (which is 16 bytes) or the destination buffer `tag` (whose size is unknown to the function, but typically expected to be at least `tag_len`).\n\nIf `tag_len` is greater than 16, `memcpy` will read out of bounds from `full_tag`. This is a buffer over-read vulnerability. The bug is introduced by the lack of bounds checking before the `memcpy` call. The specific line where the vulnerable operation occurs is line 10.\n\nAnswer: 10",
